# Shell scripts and the Dockerfile MUST be LF. Git's autocrlf on Windows would
# otherwise check them out with CRLF, and a CRLF shebang line fails inside the
# Linux container with the notoriously unhelpful:
#   exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# because the kernel treats the trailing \r as part of the interpreter path.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# The brand assets. The two font files are binary and must never be touched by
# eol conversion -- a single byte changed in an .otf and the face stops parsing.
# The logos are XML, so git WOULD treat them as text and rewrite their endings on
# a Windows checkout; harmless to the render, but it makes the diff against the
# chapter branding kit noise instead of nothing.
*.otf binary
*.woff2 binary
*.svg text eol=lf
